From db5cd9a082b746a9fd733afc7b88c72f55228a20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:19:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stage transposed selected logits in shared memory during
 normalization

Upstream-base: d20a95fd3ef5a717353475ad983ada6afd933eff, after candidate-38, selected-logit source c88a692e98 and native-input patches 0001-0006.

Rationale: late transposed-id gathers remain on the row reduction's critical path. The fixed 480-round follow-up still leaves a large BF16 case unqualified. For a transposed selection fitting one thread block, read the selected logits before the bulk reduction and retain their FP32 values in 4 KiB of shared memory. This hides dependent gather latency without the rejected global-output-buffer round trip. Other layouts and larger selections retain the existing native-input kernel.

Quality: no new CUDA launch, global buffer, dtype/layout materialization or arithmetic reordering. FP32 staging preserves the exact value consumed by final normalization. Runtime dispatch bounds the shared array; tests cover both sides of the 1024-column boundary and startup freeze. Every specialization is declared before freeze.

Tests: GPU numerical, boundary, graph, paired-performance and IKET qualification required. Recorded v6 results and its failed precision follow-up are retained in the deployment experiment.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
---
 .../test_gpu_tilelang_logprob_softmax.py      | 18 +++++--
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py | 47 +++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

